From: OpenIPC
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt7601sta: lower the cfg80211 beacon version guard for this kernel

GrainMedia backported the newer cfg80211 beacon_data/beacon_parameters fields
into this 3.3 kernel, so the (3,4,0) guard on the beacon structures in
include/rtmp_cmd.h is wrong here and the header does not compile with it
(CMD_RTPRIV_IOCTL_80211_BEACON has no member ssid_len). cfg80211drv.c already
builds its beacon handling against (3,2,0); lower the guard to match.

--- a/include/rtmp_cmd.h
+++ b/include/rtmp_cmd.h
@@ -380,7 +380,7 @@
         UINT32 beacon_head_len; /* Before TIM IE */
 		UINT32 beacon_tail_len; /* After TIM IE */
 
-#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3,4,0))
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3,2,0))
 	UCHAR *beacon_ies;
 	UINT32 beacon_ies_len;
 	UCHAR *proberesp_ies;
